  # Adjust according to input size\n\n    def forward(self, x):\n        x = self.embedding(x).view(-1, 1, 100, embed_size)\n        x = self.pool(self.conv1(x))\n        x = x.view(x.size(0), -1)\n        x = self.fc1(x)\n        return x\n```\n\n### Changes in `utils.py`\n- Removed the duplicate definition of the `load_model` function.\n\n### Updated `utils.py` Snippet\n```python\n"""\nUtility functions for saving and loading models.\n"""\nimport torch\n\ndef save_model(model, path=\'model.pth\'):\n    """Save the model to the specified path."""\n    torch.save(model.state_dict(), path)\n\ndef load_model(model, path=\'model.pth\'):\n    """Load the model from the specified path."""\n    model.load_state_dict(torch.load(path))\n```\n\nThese modifications should enhance the robustness and maintainability of the code. If you need any further adjustments or additional features, feel free to ask!'}], 'metadata': {'source': 'Programmer Code Review'}}], 'context_trace_complete': True}}], 'node_type': 'literal', 'input_count': 1, 'predecessors': ['Code Complete All Phase Loop Counter', 'Programmer Code Review', 'Code Review Phase Loop Counter', 'Programmer Code Complete'], 'successors': ['Programmer Code Review', 'Code Reviewer']} 
