s_data, split_data\\r\\r\\nfrom model import TextCNN\\r\\r\\nfrom evaluate import evaluate_model\\r\\r\\nfrom train import train_model\\r\\r\\n\\r\\r\\n\\r\\r\\n\\r\\r\\n\\r\\r\\n\\r\\r\\n\\r\\r\\n\\r\\r\\nThis is the main module to launch the program\\r\\r\\n\\r\\r\\n\\r\\r\\n\\r\\r\\n    evaluate_model(model, data_loader)  # Provide the necessary parameters for evaluation\\r\\r\\n",\n  "truncated": true,\n  "file_size": 1100,\n  "modified_ts": 1780234480.1045568,\n  "mode": "line_range"\n}{\n  "path": "utils.py",\n  "encoding": "utf-8-sig",\n  "newline": "\\r\\n",\n  "start_line": 1,\n  "end_line": 40,\n  "line_count": 40,\n  "lines_returned": 40,\n  "total_lines": 126,\n  "snippet": "\\"\\"\\"\\r\\r\\n\\r\\r\\n\\r\\r\\n\\r\\r\\nUtility functions for saving and loading models.\\r\\r\\n\\r\\r\\n\\r\\r\\n\\r\\r\\n\\"\\"\\"\\r\\r\\n\\r\\r\\n\\r\\r\\n    \\"\\"\\"Load the model from the specified path.\\"\\"\\"\\r\\r\\n\\r\\r\\n    model.load_state_dict(torch.load(path))\\r\\r\\n\\r\\r\\ndef save_model(model, path=\'model.pth\'):\\r\\r\\n\\r\\r\\n\\r\\r\\n\\r\\r\\n    \\"\\"\\"Save the model to the specified path.\\"\\"\\"\\r\\r\\n",\n  "truncated": true,\n  "file_size": 689,\n  "modified_ts": 1780234461.710132,\n  "mode": "line_range"\n}Based on the code snippets retrieved from the various files and the review comments, I will proceed with the following tasks:\n\n1. **Complete the `train_model` function in `train.py`.**\n2. **Enhance comments and docstrings in all relevant methods.**\n3. **Ensure that the overall flow and logic is maintained.**\n\n### Code Modifications\n\n#### 1. Completing `train_model` function in `train.py`\n\nThe `train_model` function is currently incomplete. I will add the necessary logic for training the model, including the optimization step and logging the training progress.\n\n#### 2. Adding Comments and Docstrings\n\nI will enhance the comments and add docstrings to the following functions:\n- `preprocess_data` in `data_preprocessing.py`.\n- `train_model` in `train.py`.\n- `evaluate_model` in `evaluate.py`.\n- `TextCNN` class in `model.py`.\n- Any other relevant functions in the modules.\n\n### Modifications\n\nLet\'s implement these changes in the respective files.\n\n#### Update `train.py`\n\n```python\n"""\nModule containing functions for training the model.\n"""\n\nfrom data_preprocessing import load_data, preprocess_data, split_data\nimport torch\n\ndef train_model(model, train_loader, criterion, optimizer, num_epochs=5):\n    """Train the TextCNN model.\n    \n    Args:\n        model: The TextCNN model to be trained.\n        train_loader: DataLoader for the training dataset.\n        criterion: Loss function.\n        optimizer: Optimizer for updating model parameters.\n        num_epochs: Number of epochs for training.\n    """\n    model.train()  # Set the model to training mode\n\n    for epoch in range(num_epochs):\n        total_loss = 0\n        for inputs, labels in train_loader:\n            optimizer.zero_grad()  # Zero the gradients\n\n            outputs = model(inputs)  # Forward pass\n            loss = criterion(outputs, labels)  # Compute loss\n            loss.backward()  # Backward pass\n            optimizer.step()  # Update parameters\n\n            total_loss += loss.item()\n\n        print(f\'Epoch [{epoch + 1}/{num_epochs}], Loss: {total_loss/len(train_loader):.4f}\')\n```\n\n#### Update `data_preprocessing.py`\n\n```python\n"""\nModule for data preprocessing.\n"""\n\nfrom sklearn.feature_extraction.text import TfidfVectorizer\n\ndef preprocess_data(data):\n    """Preprocess the data: tokenization and vectorization.\n    \n    Args:\n        data: Raw input data to be preprocessed.\n\n    Returns:\n        Processed data suitable for model training.\n    """\n    # Implement preprocessing steps here\n```\n\n#### Update `evaluate.py`\n\n```python\n"""\nModule for evaluating the model performance.\n"""\n\ndef evaluate_model(model, data_loader):\n    """Evaluate the TextCNN model.\n    \n    Args:\n        model: The trained TextCNN model.\n        data_loader: DataLoader for the evaluation dataset.\n    \n    Returns:\n        Accuracy of the model on the evaluation dataset.\n    """\n    model.eval()  # Set the model to evaluation mode\n    correct = 0\n    total = 0\n    \n    with torch.no_grad():\n        for inputs, labels in data_loader:\n            outputs = model(inputs)  # Forward pass\n            _, predicted = torch.max(outputs.data, 1)\n            total += labels.size(0)\n            correct += (predicted == labels).sum().item()  # Count correctly predicted labels.\n    \n    accuracy = correct / total\n    print(f\'Accuracy: {accuracy:.4f}\')\n    return accuracy\n```\n\n#### Update `model.py`\n\n```python\n"""\nModule defining the TextCNN model.\n"""\n\nimport torch.nn as nn\n\nclass TextCNN(nn.Module):\n    """TextCNN model for text classification.\n    \n    Args:\n        embed_size: Size of the embedding layer.\n        num_classes: Number of output classes.\n    """\n    \n    def __init__(self, embed_size=300, num_classes=2):\n        super(TextCNN, self).__init__()\n        self.embedding = nn.EmbeddingBag(10000, embed_size, sparse=True)\n        # Define other layers and architecture here\n```\n\n#### Update `main.py`\n\nEnsure that the function calls in `main.py` correctly pass the required parameters to `evaluate_model`.\n\n### Saving Changes\n\nNow I will save these changes back to their respective files.{\n  "path": "train.py",\n  "encoding": "utf-8-sig",\n  "newline": "\\r\\n",\n  "line_count": 749,\n  "applied_edits": 1,\n  "trailing_newline": true,\n  "file_size": 4338,\n  "modified_ts": 1780234530.5114272\n}{\n  "path": "data_preprocessing.py",\n  "encoding": "utf-8-sig",\n  "newline": "\\r\\n",\n  "line_count": 3108,\n  "applied_edits": 1,\n  "trailing_newline": true,\n  "file_size": 11072,\n  "modified_ts": 1780234530.5166192\n}{\n  "path": "evaluate.py",\n  "encoding": "utf-8-sig",\n  "newline": "